1
00:00:00,514 --> 00:00:08,000
ReplayLab 3.0 · Watch. Learn. Do.
Tutorials explain actions. ReplayLab checks visible results.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:20,375
This is an actual local app recording.
Workflow extraction is offline; screen OCR processes real captured pixels.

3
00:00:20,375 --> 00:00:36,952
Upload a rights-cleared tutorial and its timestamped transcript.
FFmpeg extracts real source frames. Offline extraction proposes quoted UI labels.

4
00:00:36,952 --> 00:00:52,639
One shared workflow graph: timestamps, visible conditions and prerequisites.
Review and approve the proposal before verification can begin.

5
00:00:52,639 --> 00:01:18,311
Real browser tab sharing → local OCR → evidence-backed PASS.
CodeLab is a controlled software simulation, not a real extension installation.

6
00:01:18,311 --> 00:01:32,514
A visible wrong destination produces FAIL, with actual counterevidence.
The correction points back to the approved Extensions workflow.

7
00:01:32,514 --> 00:01:46,577
Correct the visible state and the next checkpoint passes.
Progress is persisted; dependencies unlock the following step.

8
00:01:46,577 --> 00:01:53,921
Missing evidence is UNCERTAIN, not automatic failure.
Showing a different view cannot establish whether the required details are open.

9
00:01:53,921 --> 00:02:12,405
Sharing is stopped. The app now reviews fresh, actual target screenshots.
Visible CodeLab 2.0 differs from the approved source: evidence-backed UNCERTAIN.

10
00:02:12,405 --> 00:02:14,625
Manual screenshot review confirms Installed and Enabled: four of four.
ReplayLab observes visible evidence; the sandbox installation is simulated.

11
00:02:14,625 --> 00:02:25,717
Stop ends the real capture track. Screenshots are never retained.
Only opted-in, relevant redacted decision evidence is saved for inspection.

12
00:02:25,717 --> 00:02:33,936
Physical mode uses the same workflow and decision-inspection contract.
This controlled block checkpoint uses labeled fixture observations, not live SAM.

13
00:02:33,936 --> 00:02:46,061
Measured evaluation: 20/20 agreement on controlled browser captures.
Small, development-team-labeled local OCR set; not broad real-world or Meta accuracy.

14
00:02:46,061 --> 00:02:55,061
Meta Muse Spark and SAM adapters are implemented and contract-tested.
Live Meta inference and hackathon eligibility remain unverified; this demo is offline.

15
00:02:55,061 --> 00:03:00,000
ReplayLab: demonstration → expected states → evidence → verification.
Its advantage is knowing when to pass, when to correct, and when it cannot decide.
